course: dictionary
lesson: 15385
title: Speckled: covered in tiny spots
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture in your head, and speckled is one of them. When you see it, picture something covered in tiny dots or marks. «The thrush laid speckled blue eggs in the nest.» The clue is in the sentence: the eggs are blue with tiny spots, not one big stripe or one plain colour.
explain: Use the words around speckled to find its meaning. «The trout swam under the stream, its speckled sides shining in the sun.» A trout is a fish, and the sides shining tells you the spots are on its body. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Spotted or dotted might fit, so speckled is close to those words.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «its spotted sides shining in the sun» and see if it still makes sense. It does, so your guess is right. Speckled means many small marks, not one large patch.
fact: Speckled means covered with lots of small spots or marks of a different colour.
fact: Speckled is an adjective: it describes things like eggs, birds, fish or stones.
fact: In nature, speckled feathers can help an animal hide, which is called camouflage.
fact: «Five Little Speckled Frogs» is a counting rhyme that children often sing.
exercise: «The speckled hen scratched in the garden.» What does speckled mean here? | *Covered with small spots or marks | Ready to fly away | Freshly washed and clean | Very large and round
exercise: Which of these things is most likely to be speckled? | A smooth black road | A clean white sheet | *A thrush's egg with tiny brown dots | A bowl of plain white rice
exercise: «Among the leaves, the frog was hard to see.» Why was it hard to see? | *Its speckled back blended in with the leaves | It was making a loud noise | It was sitting under a bowl | It was very tiny
test: «The speckled trout swam in the cold river.» What is speckled? | The river | The swimming | The cold | *The trout
test: Which word is closest in meaning to speckled? | Shiny | Smooth | *Spotted | Quiet
exam: Which sentence uses speckled correctly? | Her shoes were speckled with black laces | The road was speckled with a long, smooth surface | The music was speckled with loud drums | *The hen's eggs were speckled with tiny brown dots
